#### Using hooks with Plan Mode


You can use the [hook system](/docs/hooks/writing-hooks) to automate parts of

the planning workflow or enforce additional checks when Gemini CLI transitions

into or out of Plan Mode.

Hooks such as `BeforeTool` or `AfterTool` can be configured to intercept the `enter_plan_mode` and `exit_plan_mode` tool calls.

When hooks are triggered by **tool executions** , they do **not** run when you manually toggle Plan Mode using the `/plan` command or the `Shift+Tab` keyboard shortcut. If you need hooks to execute on mode changes,

ensure the transition is initiated by the agent (for example, by asking "start

a plan for...").

